---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="ReadFluent Support"
  description="How to get help with ReadFluent, the bilingual e-book reader."
>
  <article>
    <header class="post-header">
      <p class="kicker">Support</p>
      <h1>ReadFluent</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        ReadFluent is a bilingual e-book reader for iPhone, iPhone Duo, and iPad. Import an EPUB
        you own, read it in the original language, and show a translation of the page when you
        need it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email
        <a href="mailto:help@readfluentapp.com">help@readfluentapp.com</a>
        and include the device you are using, the iOS version, and what you expected to happen.
      </p>

      <h2>Importing a book</h2>
      <p>
        In Library, tap Add Book and choose an EPUB. If the file is already on your shelf, the
        app tells you instead of adding it again. Deleting a book removes that file and its
        bookmarks from the device.
      </p>

      <h2>Translation</h2>
      <p>
        On a phone, use Translate to switch between the original page and the translated page. On
        a wide landscape window, such as an iPad or an open iPhone Duo, the original and the
        translation sit on facing pages. You can change the language you are reading toward from
        the reader. If a language is not installed, the system may ask to download it.
      </p>

      <h2>Bookmarks and appearance</h2>
      <p>
        A bookmark saves the passage so you can open it again later. In Settings, the page can be
        warm white, sepia, or charcoal. That choice stays on this device.
      </p>

      <p>
        How the app handles your library is described in the
        <a href="/privacy/readfluent">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <a class="back" href="/blog/readfluent">ReadFluent</a>
</Base>
